2:45.000Z","author":"dependabot[bot]","subject":"(chore) Bump jspdf from 3.0.1 to 3.0.2 (#2717)","message":"(chore) Bump jspdf from 3.0.1 to 3.0.2 (#2717)\n\nBump jspdf from 3.0.1 to 3.0.2\n\nBumps [jspdf](https://github.com/parallax/jsPDF) from 3.0.1 to 3.0.2.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/parallax/jsPDF/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/parallax/jsPDF/blob/master/RELEASE.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/parallax/jsPDF/compare/v3.0.1...v3.0.2)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: jspdf\n  dependency-version: 3.0.2\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[2717],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"8b31fe7df63e202d9b5101bc8c73f7a2c748fb09","date":"2025-07-29T19:57:09.000Z","author":"dependabot[bot]","subject":"(chore) Bump linkifyjs from 4.2.0 to 4.3.2 (#2625)","message":"(chore) Bump linkifyjs from 4.2.0 to 4.3.2 (#2625)\n\nBumps [linkifyjs](https://github.com/nfrasser/linkifyjs/tree/HEAD/packages/linkifyjs) from 4.2.0 to 4.3.2.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/nfrasser/linkifyjs/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/nfrasser/linkifyjs/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/nfrasser/linkifyjs/commits/v4.3.2/packages/linkifyjs)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: linkifyjs\n  dependency-version: 4.3.2\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[2625],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"e359da592c220eecde4552ad213e4bc2cdd8e195","date":"2025-07-04T06:41:45.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(feat) Optimize visit data revalidation to avoid SWR cache cascades (#2554)","message":"(feat) Optimize visit data revalidation to avoid SWR cache cascades (#2554)\n\n* (feat) Optimize visit data revalidation to avoid SWR cache cascades\n\nThis PR addresses performance bottlenecks in visit and encounter data management by replacing global revalidation with more targeted cache invalidation.\n\nPresently, the global `mutateVisit()` revalidation function triggers 13+ unnecessary network requests per operation, and all visit-related components are revalidated even when only specific data changed.\n\nThis approach:\n\n- Replaces the global `mutateVisit()` with targeted SWR cache invalidation to reduce 13+ revalidation requests to 1 per operation.\n- Moves revalidation utilities from the chart app to `@openmrs/esm-patient-common-lib` for better reusability.\n- Creates multiple utility functions for surgical cache invalidation:\n  - `invalidateVisitHistory()` - Only invalidates visit history table data\n  - `invalidatePatientEncounters()` - Only invalidates encounter data\n  - `invalidateVisitAndEncounterData()` - Combines both for operations affecting both\n  - `useOptimisticVisitMutations()` - Hook for optimistic updates without network requests\n- Fixes the encounter table cache invalidation regex to handle flexible URL parameter order.\n- Updates all visit/encounter operations to use surgical cache targeting:\n  - Visit creation/editing (`visit-form.workspace.tsx`)\n  - Visit deletion/restoration (`useDeleteVisit.hook.tsx`)\n  - Encounter deletion (`encounters-table.component.tsx`)\n  - Form submissions (`form-entry.workspace.tsx`)\n  - Visit note creation (`visit-notes-form.workspace.tsx`)\n  - Order basket operations (`order-basket.workspace.tsx`)\n  - Vitals/biometrics forms (`vitals-biometrics-form.workspace.tsx`)\n  - End visit dialog (`end-visit-dialog.component.tsx`)\n- Preserves current visit component performance by avoiding unnecessary revalidation.\n- Ensures the `AllEncountersTable` updates correctly after form submissions and other encounter operations.\n\nThis eliminates","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[2554],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"9a91acef9cfbc5647a5c3577f981d9496d5cf97c","date":"2025-06-05T05:24:51.000Z","author":"dependabot[bot]","subject":"(chore) Bump webpack-dev-server from 4.15.2 to 5.2.1 (#2489)","message":"(chore) Bump webpack-dev-server from 4.15.2 to 5.2.1 (#2489)\n\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[2489],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"4910e35051d4f2cd62e5c19e0eec96fe82a1f047","date":"2025-03-21T19:07:24.000Z","author":"dependabot[bot]","subject":"Bump jspdf from 2.5.1 to 3.0.1 (#2293)","message":"Bump jspdf from 2.5.1 to 3.0.1 (#2293)\n\nBumps [jspdf](https://github.com/MrRio/jsPDF) from 2.5.1 to 3.0.1.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/MrRio/jsPDF/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/parallax/jsPDF/blob/master/RELEASE.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/MrRio/jsPDF/compare/v2.5.1...v3.0.1)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: jspdf\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[2293],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"5c1b7900968554ab3820216d3c0203c46386a76d","date":"2025-03-17T16:26:16.000Z","author":"dependabot[bot]","subject":"(chore) Bump canvg from 3.0.10 to 3.0.11 (#2291)","message":"(chore) Bump canvg from 3.0.10 to 3.0.11 (#2291)\n\nBumps [canvg](https://github.com/canvg/canvg) from 3.0.10 to 3.0.11.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/canvg/canvg/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/canvg/canvg/blob/v3.0.11/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/canvg/canvg/commits/v3.0.11)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: canvg\n  dependency-type: indirect\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[2291],"linksSource":"message, unverified"}],"filters":{"repos":["github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart"],"revisions":["HEAD"],"messageTerms":["glob","dependabot","vulnerab","CVE","lockfile"],"count":30},"coverageGaps":[],"truncated":["commits: answer byte cap reached; showing 24 of 30 found"]}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6cdbde18-8884-493b-8e3d-ce6a665d6b84","uuid":"5be54287-1c81-4cd4-886f-83d5f7c9faad","timestamp":"2026-10-31T15:37:36.539Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"0803b6ebda4a7acf26659df193707d8ad8d68c61","date":"2026-10-02T09:59:36.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-6026: Prefetch the vitals charts and keep their height while they load (#3727)","message":"(fix) O3-6026: Prefetch the vitals charts and keep their height while they load (#3727)\n\n* (fix) Prefetch the vitals charts and keep their height while they load\n\nThe vitals and biometrics widgets now start loading their chart code when\nsomeone hovers over or focuses the table/chart switcher. By the time they\nclick, the chart chunk is usually ready and the chart renders without a\nloading state.\n\nWhen the chunk isn't ready yet, the fallback is now a SkeletonPlaceholder\nthe same height as the rendered chart view (466px plus margins) instead of\na one-line InlineLoading. The spinner shrank the card to a single line and\npulled the widgets below it up, then pushed them back down when the chart\nrendered. The skeleton keeps the card at its final height. It keeps\nrole=\"progressbar\" and a \"Loading\" label for screen readers.\n\n* Ignore failed chart prefetches\n\nThe hover and focus handlers returned the import promise, so a failed\nchunk download on hover became an unhandled rejection, and O3's global\nhandler showed an error toast before anyone opened the chart view.\n\nThe handlers now call a prefetch wrapper that ignores the failure.\nReact.lazy still uses the uncaught loader, so opening the chart view\nretries the download, and a failure there still reaches an error\nboundary.\n\n* Test the chart prefetch in the vitals and biometrics widgets\n\nEach widget gets two tests: hovering the table/chart switcher starts\nloading the chart module, and a failed prefetch leaves the table in\nplace without an unhandled rejection. Vitest fails the run on an\nunhandled rejection, so removing the prefetch's catch fails the suite.\n\nThe tests mock the chart module with vi.doMock and import a fresh copy\nof the widget after vi.resetModules, so each test starts with its own\nReact.lazy state and a chart module that hasn't been imported yet.\n\n---------","ticketKeys":["O3-6026"],"pullRequests":[3727],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"fb88c0c95236350bd63a216ac5f10dccf6ad3338","date":"2026-09-21T20:47:24.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(chore) O3-5924: Remove unused workspace dependencies (#3680)","message":"(chore) O3-5924: Remove unused workspace dependencies (#3680)\n\nRemove nine unused dependency declarations across eight patient chart workspaces, following Daniel’s review of #3678. Update the lockfile without changing package versions.\n\nKeep linkifyjs for linkify-react and lodash-es where patient tests uses it. All eight workspaces pass lint, type checks, production builds and 394 existing tests.","ticketKeys":["O3-5924"],"pullRequests":[3680],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"5bddd92e7e0cca2b84fdd8a9dc9936713b980a1c","date":"2026-09-21T14:23:26.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(chore) O3-5924: Remove unused React dependencies (#3678)","message":"(chore) O3-5924: Remove unused React dependencies (#3678)\n\nRemove react-barcode and react-grid-gallery. Their imports were removed when label printing and the attachments gallery changed, but the dependency declarations remained.\n\nRegenerate the lockfile without upgrading retained packages. Keep the React type fixes separate.","ticketKeys":["O3-5924"],"pullRequests":[3678],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"502b0072964465322124ab769a896c3f09aea226","date":"2026-09-09T22:38:48.000Z","author":"Ian","subject":"(fix) Patient chart shouldn't generate global CSS rules (#3634)","message":"(fix) Patient chart shouldn't generate global CSS rules (#3634)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3634],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"d94bfc3e629296ba9f4e70fdfdf66414c08bbeca","date":"2026-08-07T09:38:45.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(chore) O3-5878: Bump @angular/* to 20.3.27 to resolve Dependabot security alerts (#3554)","message":"(chore) O3-5878: Bump @angular/* to 20.3.27 to resolve Dependabot security alerts (#3554)\n\nCloses three high-severity Dependabot alerts against esm-form-entry-app:\nGHSA-jj27-h5hq-8x99 (@angular/core, @angular/compiler) and\nGHSA-jhpw-976m-542j (@angular/common). Both are fixed in 20.3.27.\n\nDependabot opened one PR per vulnerable package (#3535, #3536, #3537).\nAngular framework packages peer-depend on each other at an exact patch\nversion, so bumping a subset leaves the tree with peer ranges Yarn\nreports as non-overlapping. Each of those PRs adds two such warnings,\nand merging all three still leaves eight framework packages at 20.3.26.\nThis moves the whole train instead.\n\n@angular/cdk and @angular/material stay at 20.2.14. They track the\nComponents train and peer on a range, not an exact version.\n@angular/cli, @angular-devkit/* and @schematics/angular stay put too,\nsince they are on their own version line and already float to 20.3.32.\n\nCo-authored-by: denniskigen <dennis@openmrs.org>","ticketKeys":["O3-5878"],"pullRequests":[3554],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"26b1f7c8afb742babba4360a7b974df41c6d34dd","date":"2026-07-27T20:46:43.000Z","author":"Josephkagimu1","subject":"(chore) O3-5803: Bump @angular/* to 20.3.26 to resolve Dependabot security alerts (#3501)","message":"(chore) O3-5803: Bump @angular/* to 20.3.26 to resolve Dependabot security alerts (#3501)","ticketKeys":["O3-5803"],"pullRequests":[3501],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"23534665aa959b2921f11401aa2e275db61501f7","date":"2026-07-17T10:38:00.000Z","author":"denniskigen","subject":"(chore) Include ngx-formentry in the OpenMRS dependency auto-update","message":"(chore) Include ngx-formentry in the OpenMRS dependency auto-update\n\nThe 4-hourly updater covers the framework, the React form engine lib,\nand the openmrs tooling, but not the Angular form engine, so the\nesm-form-entry-app lockfile resolution for @openmrs/ngx-formentry@next\nfroze at 20.0.1-pre.525 while the engine kept moving (the current next\nis pre.564, carrying the ICD-11 diagnosis code display, the endpoint\ndata source, and the remote-select centering fixes). Adding the package\nto the yarn up list lets the existing automation open the catch-up PR\nand keep the Angular engine current alongside its React peer.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"07236b43cf7c34172b3221c547b89bb66dcf953b","date":"2026-07-03T12:48:51.000Z","author":"Jayasanka Weerasinghe","subject":"(chore) Revert OWASP vulnerability patches (#3442)","message":"(chore) Revert OWASP vulnerability patches (#3442)\n\n* Revert \"(chore) O3-5782: Patch OWASP-reported transitive vulnerabilities (#3436)\"\n\nThis reverts commit fca099e31febb918637cf2dc91a5e6f9b7f7ff1e.\n\n* Revert \"(fix) Patch OWASP-reported minimatch vulnerabilities (#3433)\"\n\nThis reverts commit 5ba5b70a72d0a60d3dfa6136efe8237ce118d80b.\n\n* Revert \"(chore) Resolve shell-quote security advisory (#3430)\"\n\nThis reverts commit 3484232ed02d50aa60091e1b9b355b4dd2f5f0dd.\n\n* Revert \"(fix) Patch OWASP-reported high severity dependency vulnerabilities (#3428)\"\n\nThis reverts commit 4d8052092f11fc3ff981123d7fe97e49f610c8c7.\n\n* (chore) Upgrade react-router-dom to ^6.30.4","ticketKeys":["O3-5782"],"pullRequests":[3442],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"fca099e31febb918637cf2dc91a5e6f9b7f7ff1e","date":"2026-06-30T13:36:38.000Z","author":"Jayasanka Weerasinghe","subject":"(chore) O3-5782: Patch OWASP-reported transitive vulnerabilities (#3436)","message":"(chore) O3-5782: Patch OWASP-reported transitive vulnerabilities (#3436)\n\nAdds `resolutions` overrides for transitive dependencies flagged by the\nOWASP Dependency-Check scan. Each entry pins to the latest patched version\nwithin the existing consumer's major range, so no consumer's range is\nbroken.","ticketKeys":["O3-5782"],"pullRequests":[3436],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"5ba5b70a72d0a60d3dfa6136efe8237ce118d80b","date":"2026-06-30T02:56:53.000Z","author":"Jayasanka Weerasinghe","subject":"(fix) Patch OWASP-reported minimatch vulnerabilities (#3433)","message":"(fix) Patch OWASP-reported minimatch vulnerabilities (#3433)\n\nUpgrades three pinned minimatch versions to patched releases to fix\nGHSA-23c5-xmqv-rm74, GHSA-3ppc-4f35-3m26, and GHSA-7r86-cg39-jmmj\n(all High severity, 3 CVEs × 3 affected versions = 9 total findings):\n\n- minimatch 3.1.2 → 3.1.5  (^3.x requests, e.g. glob, ignore)\n- minimatch 5.1.0 → 5.1.9  (^5.x requests)\n- minimatch 9.0.5 → 9.0.9  (^9.x requests)\n\nEach upgrade stays within its major version so API compatibility\nwith dependents is preserved.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3433],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"3484232ed02d50aa60091e1b9b355b4dd2f5f0dd","date":"2026-06-30T02:34:00.000Z","author":"Jayasanka Weerasinghe","subject":"(chore) Resolve shell-quote security advisory (#3430)","message":"(chore) Resolve shell-quote security advisory (#3430)\n\nAdd shell-quote resolution to enforce >=1.8.4, resolving CVE-2026-9277\n(critical shell command injection via unescaped newlines in .op values).\nAll three shell-quote instances (root, esm-form-entry-app, build-angular)\nnow resolve to 1.9.0.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3430],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"4d8052092f11fc3ff981123d7fe97e49f610c8c7","date":"2026-06-30T02:07:27.000Z","author":"Jayasanka Weerasinghe","subject":"(fix) Patch OWASP-reported high severity dependency vulnerabilities (#3428)","message":"(fix) Patch OWASP-reported high severity dependency vulnerabilities (#3428)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3428],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"e4ea8f481f86af95a0eb4bf384910dbe6437359e","date":"2026-03-20T18:31:19.000Z","author":"dependabot[bot]","subject":"Bump flatted from 3.2.5 to 3.4.2 (#3146)","message":"Bump flatted from 3.2.5 to 3.4.2 (#3146)\n\nBumps [flatted](https://github.com/WebReflection/flatted) from 3.2.5 to 3.4.2.\n- [Commits](https://github.com/WebReflection/flatted/compare/v3.2.5...v3.4.2)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: flatted\n  dependency-version: 3.4.2\n  dependency-type: indirect\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot]